# Spot-exchange matrix is law

Canonical product spec (UI, money, windows A–D, notifs, roles):

`docs/superpowers/specs/2029-09-20-spot-exchange-refinment.md`

(Status must stay **approved-v2** or newer approved. Plans under
`docs/superpowers/plans/` are implementation notes, not overrides.)

## Before changing exchange behaviour

1. **Read the matrix** for the cells you will touch (owner/driver × window × action).
2. **Update the MD first** — rewrite the affected cells / money table / locked
   decisions so they match the intended product. Do not leave the spec stale.
3. **Then** change domain, API, mobile UI, or i18n to match the updated MD.
4. If the user changes a product rule in chat, lock it in the MD in the same
   turn before coding.

## Never

- Invent handshake / cancel / forfeit / ready rules that contradict the matrix.
- “Quick fix” only in SpotSheet / reservation detail / Go cancel without
  updating the matching cell.
- Weaken S1–S10 or window A–D definitions without an explicit MD edit and
  status note.

## Scope examples that trigger this rule

Bilateral ready, en-route, retract, FairCancel 30m, owner cancel release (S10),
no-show clocks, SpotSheet exchange CTAs, in-app exchange notifs, reservation
status panel copy.
